{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded","id":1388887,"title":"My thoughts about Technocracy Reloaded?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-16T05:31:03-07:00","id":1388887,"title":"My thoughts about Technocracy Reloaded?","content":"This book is amazing! Probably the best Mage product I\u2019ve ever read (I\u2019ve read up to the third manuscript preview page 64). I just hope they do one just as good for the Traditions and the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> I loved what they did with the Harbingers of Avalon and the SPD. I do have two questions though.<br /> <br /> First, why is it such a mystery where the NWO came from? I thought it was pretty clear in canon that they evolved from the Cabal of Pure Thought, just like the Technocracy as a whole evolved from the Order of Reason.<br /> <br /> Second, in the third manuscript page 17 first paragraph it says \u201cIt\u2019s not unusual for a Black Suit squad to conduct their intimate connection in, shall we say, a traditionally Spartan manner.\u201d I get that this is a sexual reference, but I don\u2019t know enough about Spartan culture to get the joke. Can someone please explain it to me? (You can tell me in PM if you don\u2019t want to say it in public.) Thanks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this book is great. You should totally back the Kickstarter if you haven\u2019t already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T05:40:13-07:00","id":1388889,"title":"","content":"Hmm sounds promising, I never thought of the idea of them doing a similar book for the Traditions and the Disparate but that is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Haven't read that part of the preview but Spartan generally refers to simple and pragmatic things without adornment, so a spartan apartment could just mean you have a mattress lights and toilet paper. So maybe this line means they have quickies which are direct and to the point, like I don't know in a broomcloset or under the stairwell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T05:50:42-07:00","id":1388897,"title":"","content":"Or just quickly and efficiently masturbate to relieve the tension that kind of chemistry can cause on an already stressful mission...<br /> <br /> Thanks. Now I get it.<br /> <br /> You should back the Kickstarter if you get a chance and you like M20. It\u2019ll be out on BackerKit eventually, but that could be months from now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:47:43-07:00","id":1388915,"title":"","content":"I agree with Convention Book Void Engineers that the Dimensional Anomaly (the Avatar Storm) \u201cstarted in 1999 and still continues in a much-diminished capacity today.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:10:25-07:00","id":1388928,"title":"","content":"Yeah I have the funds so I will back it. I still have some issues with how things are run hear and the only feedback I get to give seems to be in the Kickstarter boxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:17:51-07:00","id":1388930,"title":"","content":"From what I understand, sexual relations between Spartan men was a fairly common practice. I think that's what was being referred to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:28:29-07:00","id":1388935,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> okay, thanks. That makes sense. The word Lesbian dates back to ancient Greece too.<br /> <br /> Again, I could see it being a matter of efficiency for Technocrats (if there\u2019s no one of the opposite sex around, the same sex will do in a pinch...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:33:44-07:00","id":1388938,"title":"","content":"\u2026actually, the Spartan approach \u2014 and the more PC take on the Technocracy in TR \u2014 is that it's not a case of homosexual relations being a \u201cnext best thing\u201d for agents who can't engage in regular heterosexual relations did to being in the field; it's being presented as a good thing in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T07:57:10-07:00","id":1388942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1388938#post1388938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026actually, the Spartan approach \u2014 and the more PC take on the Technocracy in TR \u2014 is that it's not a case of homosexual relations being a \u201cnext best thing\u201d for agents who can't engage in regular heterosexual relations did to being in the field; it's being presented as a good thing in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhh that kind of spartan approach.<br /> <br /> Wait so fraternization in the field is encouraged? With how regulated the Technocracy is they seem pretty loosey goosey sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T09:36:30-07:00","id":1388970,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> that works too. Being gay/lesbian is a legit choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T09:38:53-07:00","id":1388971,"title":"","content":"So is being bi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T11:47:28-07:00","id":1389015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1388942#post1388942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ohhh that kind of spartan approach.<br /> <br /> Wait so fraternization in the field is encouraged? With how regulated the Technocracy is they seem pretty loosey goosey sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's less-loosey goosey than you think. While there will be variances in each Convention and within each major section of each convention, it requires T3 status in the Technocracy to be allowed to marry and to have and children. T3 is the supervisors and managers level, so few PCs would be at that level. Anyone who is more than just an ordinary citizen who has rank in the Union will be greater than T0, an ordinary Citizen. Thus, PCs as T1 (extraordinary Citizens) or T2 (enlightened operatives) would be unable to marry.<br /> <br /> T2 members of the Technocracy are allowed relationships if their SDS (Six Degrees of Separation) is 3 or less; thus having a relationship recognized requires a showing of loyalty to the Technocracy. Direct supervisor-subordinate regulations are forbidden (somewhat overlooked in the Syndicate where the old boy's club rules) as dangerous. When you think of a chain of command, this makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> As for the other types of fraternization, well the Technocracy is looking at instead of denying everyone part of humanity like the Akashic Brotherhood or Celestial Chorus elements that focus on denial of basic human urges, it's looking to safely control them. If it's not a performance issue, the Technocracy doesn't care about your sexuality and gender.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's views on gender and sexuality are still potentially chilling. If the Technocracy really don't care and favor diversity in Masses societies which still have divisive views on those subjects, are they helping operatives who differ from the Masses in their gender and sexual orientation, or are they basically being permissive libertarians in theory who do not stand up for gender and sexual minorities? If it's just libertarianism to serve efficiency, then in some cases, I'd make the Technocracy worse than some of the Traditions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T12:58:32-07:00","id":1389049,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m confused. Why is being permissive potentially chilling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:04:55-07:00","id":1389080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1389049#post1389049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m confused. Why is being permissive potentially chilling?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find the possibility of the Technocracy being permissive chilling. What I find chilling is the control they exert over people's lives and how they use the idea of diversity and permissiveness to take control.<br /> <br /> The 'you must be this loyalty level to have a recognized relationship' and you must be this level to be allowed to have children if you want them and that all children are to spend time away from the parents and be trained in Technocracy ways are massive attacks on individual freedom. Each Technocrat has a duty to the Technocracy that trumps all else.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy really only wants people to love the <i>Technocracy. </i>I'd prefer a game where, if you're playing the good people, then the type of good people you play isn't limited by their body configuration and whom they choose to love. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T15:12:39-07:00","id":1389083,"title":"","content":"It's a form of permissiveness that's stemming from a potentially shifting rationale. When the authorities support something as a matter of practicality... that support dries up if it gets less practical.<br /> <br /> For any minority group that's been through that, the open attitude can seem like a trap; thus being chilling. If the Union doesn't care about your gender identity, it might seem like a good thing in terms of not discriminating against you because of it, but it can be a terrible thing when it comes to not caring to stand up for your gender identity when it comes under attack.<br /> <br /> It's the whole problem with the &quot;I'm not racist, I'm color-blind,&quot; mentality. While it might be great if someone truly operates in their personal decision making without bias regarding race, if they're so &quot;color-blind&quot; it just means they don't see when other people and/or institutions are being racist. It sends the signal that being a minority has no real protections; that your managers and supervisors only really care about who causes the least problems; if you're constantly reporting people for &quot;minor&quot; racist incidents you're the problem, not the culture that allows those to keep happening. So you're going to shut up, and fit in, and not feel free to express yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:16:16-07:00","id":1389101,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13680_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13680\" data-vbnamecard=\"13680\">baakyocalder</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> you guys both make some good points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:18:24-07:00","id":1389103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1389083#post1389083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a form of permissiveness that's stemming from a potentially shifting rationale. When the authorities support something as a matter of practicality... that support dries up if it gets less practical.<br /> <br /> For any minority group that's been through that, the open attitude can seem like a trap; thus being chilling. If the Union doesn't care about your gender identity, it might seem like a good thing in terms of not discriminating against you because of it, but it can be a terrible thing when it comes to not caring to stand up for your gender identity when it comes under attack.<br /> <br /> It's the whole problem with the &quot;I'm not racist, I'm color-blind,&quot; mentality. While it might be great if someone truly operates in their personal decision making without bias regarding race, if they're so &quot;color-blind&quot; it just means they don't see when other people and/or institutions are being racist. It sends the signal that being a minority has no real protections; that your managers and supervisors only really care about who causes the least problems; if you're constantly reporting people for &quot;minor&quot; racist incidents you're the problem, not the culture that allows those to keep happening. So you're going to shut up, and fit in, and not feel free to express yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>This much clearly states what I was thinking. The Technocracy is certainly nicer to minorities than they've been, but it's a long road beyond that to some utopian science fiction universe where diversity is truly celebrated when people want it to be celebrated.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T15:35:13-07:00","id":1389477,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised the Technocracy isn't like the Qunari.<br /> <br /> Sexaroids ready and willing to satisfy your biological urges. Just set up an appointment.<br /> <br /> Family is discouraged.<br /> <br /> Emotion is forbidden.<br /> <br /> The act?<br /> <br /> Sure, whenever you need it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T18:06:58-07:00","id":1389505,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> purely utilitarian?<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen I cum, hit me with the dead cat on the floor...\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-17T18:07:30-07:00","id":1389507,"title":"","content":"A line from the movie Her with Scarlett Johansson","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T19:08:07-07:00","id":1390152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1389103#post1389103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This much clearly states what I was thinking. The Technocracy is certainly nicer to minorities than they've been, but it's a long road beyond that to some utopian science fiction universe where diversity is truly celebrated when people want it to be celebrated.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The process of moving towards a more complete and authentic diversity is an ongoing thing. The Union stands at the crossroads between genuinely fighting institutional prejudices and painting over them with corporate diversity initiatives. The Collegium of Gender Studies (and the Ivory Tower as a whole) do genuinely a vested interest in improving the lives of those among the Masses that are subject to prejudice. The issue is the policy on the books and the sparse resources allocated to actually fixing those problems. <br /> <br /> I think some real nuance and intrigue can be wrung out of the political machinations between those working to repair the blindspots the Union has toward institutional power dynamics (possibly involving the DFF, one of my favorite things introduced in this book), the old-guard working to undermine what they perceive as the &quot;weakening&quot; of the Union's values in the name of diversity, and the current top brass, who will side with either depending on what will help their pet projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T21:14:54-07:00","id":1390184,"title":"","content":"Who are the DFF? Sometimes one gets lost in the acronyms.. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T23:03:22-07:00","id":1390206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1390184#post1390184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are the DFF? Sometimes one gets lost in the acronyms.. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof. Sorry, I meant the Challenge Fate Foundation, which I had misremembered as the &quot;Defy Fate Foundation&quot;, hence the acronym.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T05:14:30-07:00","id":1390259,"title":"","content":"I haven't read the book so I don't know if this fits the context, but a traditional Spartan Marriage involved the newlyweds only meeting one another in secret and at night. Basically, you were meant to sneak away at night when not training to fight and try to get to your partner without getting caught, quietly do what you do, then by morning both of you are back where you're supposed to be like nothing happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T08:27:02-07:00","id":1390295,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> wow! That\u2019s actually really hot. And way better than my other two interpretations (quickly masturbating or hooking up with another operative of the same sex even if you\u2019re not really into that cause there\u2019s no one else around). Thanks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I read Units 5 and 6 of Technocracy Reloaded last night and once again I was really impressed. I\u2019m defo glad I backed this Kickstarter. I\u2019m probably still not gonna play a Technocrat, but I have a much better idea now of how to run them as NPCs. You guys should back it if you haven\u2019t already and you like M20; I think there\u2019s like a week left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T09:09:42-07:00","id":1390303,"title":"","content":"Part of unit 7 was previewed today in update #33. There are several campaign themes, from solarpunk to cyberpunk, in that update.<br /> <br /> At $155,000, the next stretch goal, there will be a Jumpstart adventure. With the prior stretch goals unlocking the Traditions, the Disparate Alliance and street-level Orphans material to be 'Unlikely Allies,' as well as more gadgets and personnel, backing the Kickstarter will get you a huge amount of material for a Mage game.<br /> <br /> If you're going historical, well, there's a 'Weird West' theme that would nicely fit areas where railroads are being built along frontiers. I'd venture that would cross over nicely with Werewolf: The Wild West or let you explore frontiers outside the U.S. West of the 19th century. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T10:13:54-07:00","id":1390316,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13680_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13680\" data-vbnamecard=\"13680\">baakyocalder</a> that sounds great. Thanks! \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T04:22:15-07:00","id":1390527,"title":"","content":"Engineer-42 is correct that the Spartan aristocracy lived mostly gender-segregated lives for much of their adulthood. The men didn\u2019t do that much military training, though, contrary to modern depictions. Mostly they hung around reciting poetry, giving each other massages, wrestling, and brutalizing their huge slave population, since they didn\u2019t actually have jobs to do. Their marriages were arranged by the state, and they didn\u2019t live with their spouses until after \u201cretirement\u201d age. One wonders if they had much of anything to talk about at that point. Relations between them were purely for the sake of creating heirs; the women managed the estates while the men spent the vast majority of their time being idle layabouts and a little of the time leading their many vassal states in war. I expect homoerotic relationships were common, but per the Classical Greek norm, the male ones would have been pederastic. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have the Technocracy manuscript, but I expect the author was using Spartan in the general sense of \u201caustere, practical, unsentimental.\u201d With a side nod to how there\u2019s an overarching authority with job expectations that human relationships have to somehow fit into the cracks of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T04:37:12-07:00","id":1390529,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> thanks. That sounds authentic. And very Technocratic, in a way.<br /> <br /> Sparta sounds awful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T12:50:10-07:00","id":1391240,"title":"","content":"I think the way they're explaining the Technocracy and Diversity is the fact that the Technocracy is utterly free of bias.<br /> <br /> <i>Because you are not anything but a Technocrat.</i><br /> <br /> So if you come across some Nazis beating up a Jewish man/Gay person/Trans and you're of said minority, the Union doesn't expect you to care beyond your mission. This is an extreme example obviously but the implications are that your loyalties are to the Union and the Union alone.<br /> <br /> Intersectionality is not a thing.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this is not where people who want a Star Trek like future want to land so they need to work hard to reform it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T13:29:00-07:00","id":1391248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I get it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T13:33:09-07:00","id":1391252,"title":"","content":"I'm actually debating whether I'm getting it wrong myself. :LOL:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:26:38-07:00","id":1391288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1390529#post1390529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sparta sounds awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sparta was one of the few places in the ancient world where women had rights and could own property. In Athens it was forbidden to let women learn how to read. In Sparta, women were the property owners (not men) and held civil office. To quote Queen Gorgo, when asked why women in Sparta were allowed to boss men around, she said it was because only Spartan women give birth to real men. The quote was warped a bit in that movie, and Heroditus may not be the most accurate source. But putting the quote aside, it is one of many examples of how Sparta had many virtues that the other Greeks lacked.<br /> <br /> However, there are a lot of disturbing flaws they shared with other Greeks, such as chattel slavery.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:49:22-07:00","id":1391311,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25651_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25651\" data-vbnamecard=\"25651\">Marko Markoko</a> thanks!!<br /> <br /> Maybe Spartan sex isn\u2019t so bad after all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:27:11-07:00","id":1391377,"title":"","content":"n<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1390529#post1390529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> thanks. That sounds authentic. And very Technocratic, in a way.<br /> <br /> Sparta sounds awful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was. It was sort of the original proto-fascist totalitarian state, with one of the most brutal systems of slavery in history. The degree to which it\u2019s been romanticized in American media is disturbing.<br /> <br /> At the same time, Spartan women did enjoy more influence than anywhere else in the Greek world, mostly because Sparta\u2019s weird inheritance laws caused the women to end up with all the wealth. So while they couldn\u2019t vote in the assembly or hold any official position in the government, they held the purse strings. And while the men were sitting around flexing at each other, the women were running a lot of the economy behind the scenes. (The bits about Spartan women holding office and Athenian women not being able to read are <i>not </i>true, however.)<br /> <br /> The other factor is that Sparta was an aristocratic society wherein the hereditary Spartans <i>were </i>the aristocrats, and aristocratic women outranked the men of lower classes. In democratic societies, the women were just generally beneath all the men.<br /> <br /> In fact, a lot of the Spartan nonsense about being the only <i>real </i>men etc., which modern people misunderstand as referring to something military, is actually a reference to their nobility, based on the fact that they had state-owned slaves to do all the work in their society, whereas most Athenians et al. still had to work for a living, even if they did own a slave or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 05-24-2020, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T18:59:04-07:00","id":1391383,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:23:26-07:00","id":1391420,"title":"","content":"To be honest and fair, I may romanticize Sparta because that is my ancestral heritage. My great grandfather was from Vresthena. Most of my ancestors on my mother's side are Laconian. They spoke the Doric dialect of modern Greek. So a lot of mythic romanticized history was drilled into my head. Indeed, when I was about 10, I got busted stealing candy. My grandparents lectured me for hours, then a week later my grandfather taught me how to shoplift without getting caught. The tale of the Spartan boy and the fox was drilled into my head and I was taught that the true crime was getting caught. As a grown man, I do realize how ruthless the Spartans were. The Agogee was brutal. One was obligated to kill Helots and steal from them. The irony is that Spartans and Helots are now one and the same people pretty much. Probably a healthy mix of Slavic too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T01:05:39-07:00","id":1391435,"title":"","content":"Historically, I've been an anti-Spartan for a variety of reasons but kind of out of the way of this thread's subject.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T04:04:40-07:00","id":1391453,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25651_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25651\" data-vbnamecard=\"25651\">Marko Markoko</a> Spartans must have made good politicians","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T19:11:11-07:00","id":1391588,"title":"","content":"To try to veer it somewhat back onto WoD stuff: in the setting the Spartan oligarchy was the pet project of a 4th-generation Ventrue, if that tells you anything. <br /> <br /> The system was somewhat influential on Rome (another empire the Ventrue guided/parasitized), which even after its fall continued to be the defining culture of western Europe, and we all know where that went. Long story short, eventual heartland of the Order or Reason and the cultural hegemony that fostered the Technocracy. So, in short, the Ventrue are ultimately responsible for the Technocracy! (Joking, of course, but not entirely.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T19:32:42-07:00","id":1391593,"title":"","content":"I admit to mostly thinking of Sparta as a failed state due to its inability to conquer new territories due to its excessive reliance on slavery as well as constant fear of revolt. Also, its complete inability to integrate other peoples.<br /> <br /> Also overspecialization in military matters that left its economy a wreck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T19:42:43-07:00","id":1391596,"title":"","content":"I could make a joke about who was in charge of the Spartan economy; but that would be sexist and in bad taste. And almost certainly wrong in its implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T20:47:33-07:00","id":1391608,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar352_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"352\" data-vbnamecard=\"352\">Black Flag</a> fascinating. I didn\u2019t know that.<br /> <br /> Is it true in official canon that Romulus the founder of Rome was a Fourth Generation Ventrue or was that something my V:tM ST made up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T21:19:50-07:00","id":1391624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1391593#post1391593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit to mostly thinking of Sparta as a failed state due to its inability to conquer new territories due to its excessive reliance on slavery as well as constant fear of revolt. Also, its complete inability to integrate other peoples.<br /> <br /> Also overspecialization in military matters that left its economy a wreck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, they conquered all of Laconia and Messenia pretty early, which made them the main hegemonic power in the Peloponnese. Their economy was awesome by archaic standards, being entirely agrarian and slave run, which let the Spartans life like kings without lifting a finger. But their extreme conservatism kept them from ever adapting to changing times, and they never wanted to be <i>more </i>than that. Also, they were generally reluctant to engage militarily, lest their slaves revolt while they were away, and the Spartans proper were a very small population they couldn\u2019t afford to lose. They had their vassals do most of the fighting, albeit with Spartan commanders. The legendary 300 at Thermopylae were actually around 7000; the Spartans just didn\u2019t count everyone else because, you know, they weren\u2019t <i>real </i>people. <br /> <br /> As for Romulus, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>. I think that was your ST\u2019s own idea. I believe Rome in the WoD is supposed to have been fostered by Etruscan Ventrue after it was founded by mortals. Basically, the Ventrue diaspora kept trying to recreate the Second City, with them in charge. Then at some point the Lasombra and Malkavians got involved.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure what mages were up to then. I don\u2019t think we ever got a look at their ancient history, prior to the medieval period. But certainly a long time before the Technocracy, which I think is an early modern development even in its most basic form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T21:41:32-07:00","id":1391630,"title":"","content":"We're told a little bit about mages in ancient Egypt: specifically, that they organized into two groups that we're the earliest example of what would eventually become the Traditions and Technocracy, and served as the roots of the Order of Hermes. They're also supposedly the reason why there are nine Spheres, as they pioneered a nine-fold division of magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T07:22:59-07:00","id":1391676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1391630#post1391630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're told a little bit about mages in ancient Egypt: specifically, that they organized into two groups that we're the earliest example of what would eventually become the Traditions and Technocracy, and served as the roots of the Order of Hermes. They're also supposedly the reason why there are nine Spheres, as they pioneered a nine-fold division of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I\u2019m looking at Mage: the Ascension again after a good number of years, so there\u2019s a lot I\u2019ve missed. The Egyptian origin of the Order of Hermes makes sense. Also, I see that the Craftmasons (i.e. proto-Syndicate) trace their origins back to an ancient Roman group. What would we do without the White Wolf Wiki?<br /> <br /> It seems that, while Technocratic ideology came together and factionalized in the early modern, certain tendencies were always there, probably from the very beginning. It\u2019s just that modernity provided a framing for real high-stakes conflict.<br /> <br /> The question of the \u201cWesternness\u201d the Technocracy is interesting because on the one hand it pretty much has to represent the cultural imperialism of certain Western European ideologies in the modern period. On the other hand, I can see how the core tendencies that gave birth to the Technocracy would have to be more or less universal. And it\u2019s pretty much a global thing now, which means a lot of diverse groups would have to be a part of it by now. Global cultural hegemony isn\u2019t a one-way street, after all. Things be complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T10:31:54-07:00","id":1391710,"title":"","content":"Spartan style fascism pretty much describes House Tremere in Ars Magica (the current edition anyway). In fact, this discussion has given me ideas on how to use the Tremere as an adversary that is *not* some sort of undead. I sorta prefer to ignore the legacy of the oWoD and just focus on M20. But anyway. What I am thinking of is a fascist secret society, kind of like Hydra in the MCU and current Marvel comics. The Tremere have their tendrils in both the Traditions *and* Technocracy. They orchestrate the Ascension War in a complex chess game with the goal of creating a fascist utopian order.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T11:50:52-07:00","id":1391740,"title":"","content":"Speaking of separating M20 from oWoD: what do we <i>know</i> about the history of the Special Projects Division? When was it founded, and why? (I have a particular bit of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009152-spd-a-new-take\">head-canon involving the SPD</a>, and I'm wondering if it conflicts with published material.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T15:04:57-07:00","id":1391785,"title":"","content":"In an alternate universe, what might House Tremere have done, instead of dabbling in vampirism, to achieve its goals? It\u2019s a good question. And yeah, the Order of Hermes certainly includes elements of what would become Technocratic thought, only not quite enough to fit in with their modern expression. I could see a rogue house bringing that divide. Or doing a third thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T18:47:14-07:00","id":1391824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1391740#post1391740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of separating M20 from oWoD: what do we <i>know</i> about the history of the Special Projects Division? When was it founded, and why? (I have a particular bit of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1009152-spd-a-new-take\">head-canon involving the SPD</a>, and I'm wondering if it conflicts with published material.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I always felt that getting rid of the SPD was a really bad decision for multiple reasons. The Convention books seem to have done it because they felt very much apologetic and player-friendly so having an entire methodology being Nephandus would have been problematic.<br /> <br /> But it's SO COOL and gave a wonderful baddie to fight! It renders Invictus unnecessary.<br /> <br /> I also felt it's one of the best bits of crossover in the setting. OF COURSE the Syndicate would be hand-in-pocket with Pentex! They couldn't really claim to control finance in the world if they didn't have influence with the world's largest manufacturers of everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T19:24:39-07:00","id":1391837,"title":"","content":"Two points: first, the Syndicate didn't get rid of the SPD; the SPD up and disappeared on them, leaving the Syndicate baffled about what just happened. There's a lot that can be done with that. <br /> <br /> But second, that doesn't answer my question: when and how was it founded? And when did it get in bed with Pentex? Do we know for a fact that it's always been Wyrm-infested since it was established, or is it possible that it started out as something else and was gradually subverted over the years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T00:20:36-07:00","id":1391876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1391837#post1391837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But second, that doesn't answer my question: when and how was it founded? And when did it get in bed with Pentex? Do we know for a fact that it's always been Wyrm-infested since it was established, or is it possible that it started out as something else and was gradually subverted over the years?</div> </div> </div> </div>WW Wiki to the rescue: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Special_Projects_Division_(MTAs\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Sp...Division_(MTAs</a>)<br /> <br /> EDIT: It also hints on the disambiguity page that SPD gets mentioned in the WTA gameline, though there is no existing page to tell what WTA books it appears in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-27-2020, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T03:26:55-07:00","id":1391887,"title":"","content":"I think the SPD is fascinating and I\u2019d love to investigate the mystery of its disappearance if we ever end up playing our Mage campaign again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:10:17-07:00","id":1391897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1391837#post1391837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two points: first, the Syndicate didn't get rid of the SPD; the SPD up and disappeared on them, leaving the Syndicate baffled about what just happened. There's a lot that can be done with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the developers getting rid of the SPD. Poof, suddenly, they're gone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But second, that doesn't answer my question: when and how was it founded? And when did it get in bed with Pentex? Do we know for a fact that it's always been Wyrm-infested since it was established, or is it possible that it started out as something else and was gradually subverted over the years? </div> </div> </div>Sorry, my bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:52:15-07:00","id":1391933,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> yes, but there\u2019s still room to tell stories about the SPD within that context. Unlike the Merovingians, who literally just disappeared one day and the rest of the Celestial Chorus basically just forgot about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T07:59:09-07:00","id":1391938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388887-my-thoughts-about-technocracy-reloaded?p=1391933#post1391933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> yes, but there\u2019s still room to tell stories about the SPD within that context. Unlike the Merovingians, who literally just disappeared one day and the rest of the Celestial Chorus basically just forgot about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone should make a thread about all the various groups killed off in the setting becaus